00:00:51.540 --> 00:00:57.640
take the first question. And your first question today comes from the line of Peter Fedult from

00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:06.010
BNP Paribas. Please go ahead. Thanks, Peter Fedult, BNP Paribas. I realise there's not much

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:10.410
incremental you can say re-upfunding phase 3 readouts, and I heard your comments on Delbrecht

00:01:10.410 --> 00:01:12.770
Spires. So with that in mind, can we focus?

00:01:12.810 --> 00:01:17.790
Based on the accelerated approval potential for VotaPlan in Huntington's, I know phase 3

00:01:17.790 --> 00:01:23.710
planning underway, but do you have any visibility or ballpark timelines you can give us for when

00:01:23.710 --> 00:01:28.770
FDA might make a decision on whether you can file early on the phase 2 data generated thus far?

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:35.090
Thank you. Yeah, thanks, Peter. So we're planning in the process of engaging with the FDA

00:01:35.090 --> 00:01:42.150
on that phase 2 data. I think at this point, our base case remains that we would need to do the

00:01:42.150 --> 00:01:42.790
phase 3 study. We're going to do the phase 3 study on the phase 2 data. We're going to do the

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:43.150
phase 4 study on the phase 2 data. So we're going to do the phase 3 study on the phase 2 data.

00:01:43.150 --> 00:01:46.890
So we're going to do the phase 2 study on the phase 2 data. So no change on that expectation.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:51.330
I don't have a specific timeline. I would expect it to happen in the second half to provide more

00:01:51.330 --> 00:01:55.850
clarity. And I would also note that we continuously follow these phase 2 patients for

00:01:55.850 --> 00:02:02.330
a longer duration as well, which could provide us additional data. You know, we do know the FDA's

00:02:02.330 --> 00:02:09.710
recent decisions or recent guidances from some of other therapies that are available for—that

00:02:09.710 --> 00:02:12.770
could be available for Huntington's disease, which certainly, I think, is something that we

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:19.790
I think, shows the FDA's openness if the data ultimately is compelling. So we certainly want

00:02:19.790 --> 00:02:23.550
to have that engagement, but I wouldn't change our base case at this point that a phase three

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:31.830
